  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis PR is the second slice of the HEIDENHAIN Klartext (`.H`) reader in `camcraft-gcode` (first slice: #4361). The reader now reads back every block that our Klartext post writes today (#4395 cycles; #4442 cycle 32).\n\n- New module `crates/gcode/src/klartext/taps.rs`: `CYCL DEF 206` (tapping with a floating tap holder) and `CYCL DEF 207` (rigid tapping).\n  - Motion of both cycles: rapid to the set-up clearance, feed to the thread depth, feed back out to the set-up clearance, rapid to the 2nd set-up clearance when it is higher. This is the G84 chain of `cycle_expand`.\n  - 206 reads Q200, Q201, Q206, Q211, Q203, Q204. Q211 is the dwell at the bottom (`cl::Cycle` dwell). The record is `CycleKind::FloatingTap`.\n  - 207 reads Q200, Q201, Q239, Q203, Q204. The feed is S x Q239 with the S that is active at the call. The record is `CycleKind::Tap`.\n- New module `crates/gcode/src/klartext/old_cycles.rs`: the sub-block cycles.\n  - `CYCL DEF 9.0` / `9.1 DWELL <s>`: one `DwellEvent` at the `9.1` block (the cycle is DEF-active).\n  - `CYCL DEF 32.0` / `32.1 [T<mm>]` / optional `32.2 HSC-MODE:<0|1> [TA<deg>]`: checked, no change to the path.\n  - The order of the sub-blocks is enforced. A block between `9.0` and `9.1` (or `32.0` and `32.1`) is refused with its line and block number.\n- `cycles.rs`: the cycle definition has a `HoleShape` (drill, floating tap, rigid tap). The Q-list check and the hole levels are shared helpers now.\n- `cl::Cycle::entry_z` of a Klartext hole cycle is now the surface Q203. The first slice wrote the set-up clearance. Q203 is what the post's CL stream records as `ENTRY`.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/2227-klartext-reader.md`, new section \"second slice\".\n\n### Refused (by name, with the line; the message starts with `block N:`)\n\n- `CYCL DEF 207` with a negative Q239 (left-hand thread): `CYCL DEF 207 Q239`. The control turns the spindle against M3 for it, and the reader output has only the modal spindle direction.\n- `CYCL DEF 207` called without a spindle speed S above 0 (invalid cycle).\n- Q parameters that a cycle does not have, missing required ones, Q201 not negative, negative clearances, a zero pitch, a zero feed, a negative or too long dwell.\n- Sub-block cycles other than 9 and 32 (`CYCL DEF 1.0`, `7.0`, `10.0`, ...).\n- All other functions of the first slice stay refused (`RND`, `CHF`, `LP`, `CP`, `APPR`, `DEP`, `LBL`, `CALL`, `RL`, `RR`, INCH programs, ...).\n\n## Tests\n\nAll tests are in the existing directory suite `crates/gcode/tests/klartext` (two new sub-modules, no new top-level binary).\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `klartext_cycle_golden_reads_back_into_the_stream_motion_and_cycles`: the recorded golden `picomax_cycles.nc` reads back into the motion of its CL stream `cycles.cnc` (5 sections: drill, peck, deep with dwell, rigid tap, floating tap). Each stream section is a contiguous run of the read moves, and the moves between the runs are rapid approach moves above the section start. The cycle records match the stream `CYCLE` lines (kind, XY, R, bottom, entry, dwell). The cycle 9 dwell is 0.3 s after the last infeed.\n- `klartext_every_post_golden_reads_back_without_a_refused_block`: each `.nc` file in `crates/post/tests/recorded/golden/heidenhain-klartext/` parses. No block is refused, so the list of refused blocks is empty. When #4442 merges, its `picomax_smoothing.nc` comes into this test automatically.\n- `klartext_cycle_207_taps_at_s_times_pitch_and_feeds_out_to_the_set_up_clearance`\n- `klartext_cycle_206_feeds_at_q206_with_the_bottom_dwell_at_each_m99`\n- `klartext_cycle_207_needs_a_spindle_speed_at_the_call`\n- `klartext_tapping_cycle_definitions_are_checked_by_name_and_block`\n- `klartext_cycle_9_dwells_where_it_is_defined`\n- `klartext_cycle_32_is_checked_and_leaves_the_path_unchanged`\n- `klartext_sub_block_cycles_must_be_complete_and_in_order`\n- Degenerate input: `klartext_every_truncation_of_the_golden_is_refused_without_a_panic` now covers both goldens; new `klartext_seeded_mutations_of_the_cycle_golden_never_panic` (3000 seeded mutations, time limit); `klartext_bad_numbers_are_refused` has 4 more cases.\n\n## Gate results\n\nHead `16f638efb`, base `origin/main` 1cf7390dc, Windows lane `winbuild` (lanes, `--needs gcode`), `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=5`. Log: `gate-2227-16f638efb.log` (first line `head 16f638efbddaa88ea035771762e44eacd097921f`).\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: gcode build (`--no-run`) | ok (13 s) |\n| gcode suites: lib | ok |\n| gcode suites: klartext (whole suite, all pinning tests above) | ok |\n| `cargo clippy -p camcraft-gcode --all-targets -- -D warnings` | ok |\n| Example catalog suites | not applicable: no post and no toolpath generator changed |\n| Light lane / heavy lanes | not run: no crate depends on `camcraft-gcode`, so the diff reaches no `app` or `motion` lane and no light twin |\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real TNC-written program was read. The hand-written test programs follow the public manual syntax.\n- The golden of #4442 (`picomax_smoothing.nc`) is not on `main` yet. Cycle 32 is tested with hand-written blocks in the same form as the post writes them.\n- No app command, MCP tool or CLI verb reads `.H` files yet. This PR adds no user-facing command, so no MCP tool is necessary.\n- Still open on #2227: `LBL` / `CALL LBL`, `RND` / `CHF`, polar `LP` / `CP`, `APPR` / `DEP`, inch programs, `RL` / `RR`, left-hand rigid tapping. The reader refuses each of them by name.\n\nChangelog: camcraft-gcode reads HEIDENHAIN Klartext tapping cycles 206 and 207, the cycle 9 dwell and the cycle 32 tolerance, so every program that the Klartext post writes reads back.\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #2227\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
